\title{Classification identifier conventions}
\description{
All functions that accept a classification name (`from`, `to`, `classification`,
etc.) use a **single string** identifier -- not two separate `system`/`version`
parameters. Identifiers are **case-insensitive** (converted to uppercase
internally) but must match a canonical name exactly; unrecognised identifiers
raise an error of class `rcl_invalid_classification`.

## Naming pattern

Canonical identifiers follow the pattern `SYSTEM_LEVEL_VERSION`:

| Part      | Examples                                                       |
|-----------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| SYSTEM    | `NIS`, `NUTS`, `POSTAL`, `NBB`                                 |
| LEVEL     | `MUNICIPALITY`, `DISTRICT`, `PROVINCE`, `REGION`, `COUNTRY`, `LAU` |
| VERSION   | `2019`, `2025`, `2021`, `2027`, `BEFORE_2019`                  |

When the level is unambiguous (`POSTAL` has only one level, `NUTS_COUNTRY` has no
version variants), the extra parts are omitted.

## NIS classifications (Statbel)

Organised **by level**. Every level exists in three versions
(`BEFORE_2019`, `2019`, `2025`) except the version-invariant country level;
the versions differ only by the 2019/2025 commune-merger waves (province and
region boundaries are stable across versions).

| Level        | Identifiers (per version)                                                        | Description |
|--------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------|
| Municipality | `NIS_MUNICIPALITY_BEFORE_2019`, `NIS_MUNICIPALITY_2019`, `NIS_MUNICIPALITY_2025` | Communes; versions reflect the merger waves |
| District     | `NIS_DISTRICT_BEFORE_2019`, `NIS_DISTRICT_2019`, `NIS_DISTRICT_2025`             | Arrondissements |
| Province     | `NIS_PROVINCE_BEFORE_2019`, `NIS_PROVINCE_2019`, `NIS_PROVINCE_2025`             | Provinces (Brabant split: `20001` Vlaams-Brabant / `20002` Brabant wallon; Brussels pseudo-province `4000`) |
| Region       | `NIS_REGION_BEFORE_2019`, `NIS_REGION_2019`, `NIS_REGION_2025`                   | Regions (Flemish `2000`, Walloon `3000`, Brussels `4000`) |
| Country      | `NIS_COUNTRY`                                                                    | Belgium (NIS code `1000`) -- version-invariant |

## NUTS classifications (Eurostat)

Organised **by level**, mirroring the NIS layout. The NUTS 3/2/1 levels exist
in two versions (`2021`, `2027`); the LAU and country levels are
version-invariant in this package.

| Level              | Identifiers (per version)                  | Description |
|--------------------|--------------------------------------------|-------------|
| LAU / Municipality | `NUTS_MUNICIPALITY_2021`                   | Local Administrative Units; in Belgium a 1:1 bijection with `NIS_MUNICIPALITY_2019` (same territory, Eurostat coding) |
| District (NUTS 3)  | `NUTS_DISTRICT_2021`, `NUTS_DISTRICT_2027` | NUTS level 3 |
| Province (NUTS 2)  | `NUTS_PROVINCE_2021`, `NUTS_PROVINCE_2027` | NUTS level 2 |
| Region (NUTS 1)    | `NUTS_REGION_2021`, `NUTS_REGION_2027`     | NUTS level 1 |
| Country (NUTS 0)   | `NUTS_COUNTRY`                             | Belgium (`BE`) -- version-invariant |

